  academy_program_h2: "From coaching to concert",
  academy_program_p1: "Every musician who joins the Academy goes through an intensive journey under the personal guidance of violinist Karen Su and pianist Ruben Plazier. The program is built around private lessons and joint rehearsals, focused on technique, performance skill and musical depth.",
  academy_program_p2: "The preparation culminates in a try-out concert: a stage to put what's been learned into practice, and to receive feedback from fellow students and teachers before the main performances. What follows is the tour itself, with performances ranging from intimate chamber halls to large, renowned stages such as the Concertgebouw Amsterdam, Concertgebouw Bruges, the Philharmonie Luxembourg, the Elbphilharmonie Hamburg and the Musikverein Vienna.",
  academy_program_p3: "Every journey is tailor-made, matching the musician's level and ambitions. It's more than a series of concerts: it's the chance to experience the life of a touring classical musician first-hand, with all the challenges and highlights that shape a professional music career.",
  academy_origin_eyebrow: "How it began",
  academy_origin_quote: "\"What matters most isn't the great halls themselves, but the encounter with what an artist's life really involves.\" (Ruben Plazier)",
  academy_origin_p: "The idea took shape while Karen Su and Ruben Plazier were coaching gifted young musicians: the most important lessons aren't only learned in the practice room, but on the road. In small halls, during long journeys, and by playing together as an equal chamber-music partner rather than an accompanied soloist. That's how the idea arose to bring young musicians along on tour, not as spectators, but as participants.",
  academy_docenten_eyebrow: "Faculty",
  academy_docenten_h2: "Karen Su & Ruben Plazier",
  academy_docenten_p: "Karen Su is a laureate of the 2024 Queen Elisabeth Competition and, since the 2025/26 academic year, teaches violin at the Royal Conservatory of Mons; Ruben Plazier curates the classical programming for De Doelen Rotterdam and Muziekgebouw Eindhoven. Their own training, under legendary mentors such as Augustin Dumay and Jean-Bernard Pommier, shapes how they teach today: personal, demanding, and attentive to the musician behind the instrument.",
  academy_docenten_link: "Read their full story →",
  academy_details_eyebrow: "Practical details",
  academy_details_h2: "What a performance looks like",
  academy_details_p1: "As part of the journey, the young musician gets the unique opportunity to open the evening's program as a pre-concert performance. Each performance lasts around 10 minutes; the repertoire is carefully chosen in consultation with Karen Su and Ruben Plazier, matching the level of the evening.",
  academy_details_p2: "Professional photos of the performance are part of the journey, and a video recording can also be arranged.",
  academy_details_p3: "Every journey is unique: exact dates, venues and participants depend on the availability of halls and artists.",
  academy_gallery_eyebrow: "In the moment",
  academy_gallery_h2: "Moments from previous editions",
  academy_signup_eyebrow: "Apply",
  academy_signup_h2: "Apply for the Academy",
  academy_signup_lede: "Tell us about yourself and your instrument. We'll personally get in touch to discuss the possibilities.",
  academy_signup_note: "Applying goes through the Academy's application portal: fill in your details and share a recent video of your playing, so Karen Su and Ruben Plazier can review your application personally.",
  academy_signup_cta: "Go to the application portal →",
  form_naam: "Name",
  form_email: "Email address",
  form_telefoon: "Phone number",
  form_instrument: "Instrument",
  academy_form_bericht_label: "Tell us about yourself",
  academy_form_placeholder: "Training, repertoire, experience, and what you hope to achieve with the Academy...",
  academy_form_submit: "Submit application",

  overons_title: "About us | Experience Klassiek",
  overons_meta_description: "Experience Klassiek was founded by violinist Karen Su and pianist Ruben Plazier: the story behind the concert series and academy.",
  overons_eyebrow: "About us",
  overons_h1: "Two musicians, one mission",
  overons_lede: "In 2022, violinist Karen Su and pianist Ruben Plazier founded Experience Klassiek: a concert series that redefines the classical music experience through thoughtful storytelling and genuine connection with the audience, and later also an Academy, in which they pass on what they themselves received from their own teachers.",
  overons_piano_label: "Piano",
  overons_ruben_p1: "Ruben Plazier (Delft, 1998) is a classical pianist formed in the tradition of the Russian piano school. At fourteen he began at the Rotterdam Conservatory under Stéphane De May, who introduced him to French pianist Jean-Bernard Pommier, a meeting that would change his playing for good. After years of traveling between Rotterdam, Béziers and Paris, he was unanimously awarded his Diplôme Supérieur de Concertiste at the École Normale de Musique Alfred Cortot.",
  overons_ruben_p2: "As a soloist, he has performed concertos with orchestra and appeared in halls including the Concertgebouw Amsterdam and De Doelen Rotterdam, as well as in New York and Los Angeles. Beyond the stage, he curates the classical programming for De Doelen Rotterdam (season 2026/27) and Muziekgebouw Eindhoven.",
  overons_ruben_link: "Visit rubenplazier.com →",
  overons_viool_label: "Violin",
  overons_karen_p1: "Karen Su, an acclaimed violinist from Los Angeles, captivates audiences worldwide with her exceptional artistry and expressive playing. Born into a musical family, her musical journey began under her father's guidance and later flourished under Igor and Vesna Gruppman at the Rotterdam Conservatory, where she began her degree at just fifteen and graduated summa cum laude. Her artistic development reached new heights as an artist-in-residence at the Queen Elisabeth Music Chapel, mentored by the legendary Augustin Dumay.",
  overons_karen_p2: "Praised for her \"confidence and drive… warmth and intensity\" (The Strad), Karen Su has won prestigious prizes: laureate of the Queen Elisabeth Competition, special prize winner at the Wieniawski International Violin Competition, and top prize winner at both the Lipizer and Princess Astrid International Competitions. She has performed with orchestras including the Orchestre Philharmonique Royal de Liège, the Belgian National Orchestra and the Trondheim Symphony Orchestra & Opera, in halls including the Concertgebouw Amsterdam, Palais des Beaux-Arts Brussels and the Rudolfinum in Prague.",
  overons_karen_p3: "As a chamber musician, she has collaborated with artists including Augustin Dumay, Gary Hoffman, Jian Wang, Lorenzo Gatto, Miguel da Silva and Jean-Claude Vanden Eynden. Together with Ruben Plazier she forms a violin-piano duo, with whom she organizes the concert series Experience Klassiek. Karen Su currently performs on a 1747 Nicolo Gagliano violin, generously loaned by an anonymous donor.",
  overons_quote_eyebrow: "Since 2022",
  overons_quote: "Together they bring a fresh, dynamic view of classical music, connecting deeply with audiences across Europe.",
  overons_more_eyebrow: "Want to know more?",
  overons_more_h2: "Discover the concerts and the Academy",

  contact_title: "Contact | Experience Klassiek",
  contact_meta_description: "Get in touch with Experience Klassiek, Karen Su & Ruben Plazier, active in the Netherlands and Belgium.",
  contact_eyebrow: "Contact",
  contact_h1: "Get in touch",
  contact_lede: "Questions about the concert series, the Academy, or a collaboration? Karen Su and Ruben Plazier would love to hear from you.",
